### Limitations the authors admit
- 2012A&A...548A..69N: Vibrationally excited emission unresolved at ~1.7"x1.2"; maser nature needs confirmation
- 2012ApJ...754L..17Z: All hypotheses need further high-resolution sensitive observations
- 2012ApJ...760L..25E: Clumps mostly unresolved; higher resolution needed; short spacings needed
- 2012ApJ...760L..25E: Inclination of the arm is uncertain
- 2013A&A...555A..73K: Band 7 data heavily spatially filtered, redshifted wind not detected, wind age may be underestimated
- 2013AJ....146...47I: Missing flux for emission >6''; HCN 4-3 sub-thermal conclusion depends on it
- 2013ApJ...764L..14Z: Disk mass is only a lower limit with factor of five uncertainty
- 2013ApJ...769L..12L: CO data are scarce and heterogeneous; masking removes faint diffuse emission
- 2013ApJ...770L..27F: Mass estimates not corrected for non-circular motions; likely lower limits; beam smears out SMBH effect
- 2013ApJ...770L..27F: Unclear how much HCN is radiatively excited
- 2013ApJ...774L...7M: Continuum may be contaminated by line emission; noise higher in strong lines
- 2013ApJ...776...77K: Inner radius only an upper limit; brightness exponent ill-determined; full radiative transfer model postponed
- 2013MNRAS.430L..10L: Ambient CO emission poorly recovered, so fluxes are underestimated
- 2014A&A...567A.119S: Disk and outflow models cannot be distinguished at the available resolution
- 2014A&A...568A..92M: Knot C in rest-frame optical poorly fitted by the lens model
- 2014A&A...569A..11S: Extended emission resolved out; H13CO+ linewidths are lower limits; missing flux affects abundances.
- 2014AJ....147..141H: Interferometer-only data resolves out structure larger than 9.1"
- 2014ApJ...783L..13P: Emission may be partly optically thick so asymmetries may not trace mass; masses are lower limits.
- 2014ApJ...784...78R: Cannot tell whether gas lies in front of or behind the BCG
- 2014ApJ...785L..12C: Chi2 depends on non-independent error bars; fits degenerate with h_c
- 2014ApJ...787..112C: LTE, no radiative pumping, constant source size assumed; some species optically thick
- 2014ApJ...790..160S: Outflow quantities order-of-magnitude; XCO and line ratio uncertain
- 2014ApJ...791...20R: Sample biased toward brightest disks; dust opacity absolute values unconstrained
- 2014ApJ...791L...6W: Disk size near largest recoverable scale; imaginary scatter at long baselines may indicate asymmetry needing higher resolution
- 2014ApJ...792L..25V: Dust-trap effect on gas temperature not modelled
- 2014ApJ...795..156W: Small sample, selection effects, superposition and low-number statistics
- 2014ApJ...796..120W: Resolution and S/N insufficient for detailed modeling; CO fluxes unreliable due to cloud confusion; B inclination unknown
- 2014ApJ...796..131O: Missing flux on large scales biases rotation velocities at large radii
- 2014ApJ...796..131O: SO is optically thick so density and abundance unconstrained
- 2014ApJS..214....1U: Assumed uniform CO line ratio and alpha_CO give uncertain masses; interferometric masses sometimes exceed single-dish
- 2014PASJ...66...75T: Low S/N and limited resolution hinder precise classification
- 2014PASJ...66..106H: Model assumes a saturated maser and collisional pumping only, with superseded collision rates
- 2014Sci...345.1584B: Preliminary LTE model not fully optimized for ALMA; abundance uncertainties exclude free-free contamination and dust property uncertainties
- 2015A&A...584A..42A: Higher resolution needed to disentangle HCN-VIB from HCO+ blending in ULIRGs
- 2015ApJ...798...85P: Gas mass is a crude estimate, dominated by assumed isotopic ratios and temperature
- 2015ApJ...801...63M: Error maps too optimistic; negative bowl from missing short spacings; region 6 fluxes highly uncertain due to absorption
- 2015ApJ...803...97S: Many lines blended; Hot Core v_t=2 T_rot not determinable
- 2015ApJ...804...37L: Kinematic analysis preliminary since arm inclinations unknown
- 2015ApJ...806...17R: Warm-gas mass per nucleus uses global Herschel ratio
- 2015ApJ...810..112O: Model is not tuned to IM Lup, so no quantitative comparison is possible
- 2015ApJ...810..112O: Outer-ring intensity is model dependent and may vary from disk to disk
- 2015ApJ...811...39I: 150 pc resolution mixes AGN and SB contributions; CO(3-2) only partially covered
- 2015ApJ...811...92C: Model is parametric, not dynamically consistent, no systematic parameter search
- 2015ApJ...811...92C: MEM resolution varies with image
- 2015ApJ...811L...4Z: Deeper observations are needed to refine the kinematic interpretation
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: Inclination poorly constrained by the disk model; mass estimates are uncertain by optical depth, temperature, abundance
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: PV mean-position method underestimates break radius at limited resolution
- 2015ApJ...813..118M: Only three regions; nuclear HCN cut off by bandpass; single-component fit poor for Enuc. 2
- 2015ApJ...813L..19J: Gaussian fit underestimates the actual disk size
- 2015ApJ...815..103B: Different uv coverage between CARMA and ALMA makes CO line ratios uncertain; CARMA may resolve out flux
- 2015ApJ...815..106H: Uniform excitation and chemistry assumed over space and velocity; C18O contaminated; resolution too low to resolve outflow or inner structure
- 2015MNRAS.447.3936M: Detailed chemical modelling beyond scope; T_k assumed uniform; vibrational/electronic states neglected
- 2015Natur.522..455C: Dynamical masses very uncertain due to low spatial resolution
- 2015Natur.525..218R: NW ALMA flux is lower than APEX; may reflect different line ratio, weak emission or resolved-out extended emission
- 2016A&A...587A..91B: Uniform single-component LTE model cannot fit very optically thick lines; formal temperature errors unreliable
- 2016A&A...590A..73A: Resolution is insufficient for proper model fits; the jet mass is uncertain because of the CO-to-H2 conversion factor
- 2016A&A...592A..76D: Only 16-20 antennas; cannot prove either scenario
- 2016A&A...594A..81P: Factor ~5 systematic uncertainty in mass from alpha_CO; masses are lower limits
- 2016A&A...594A..81P: Origin of outflowing molecular gas unclear from available data
- 2016A&A...596A..88L: Detailed radiative transfer disk modelling and SED fitting beyond scope; mass estimates are simple
- 2016A&A...596A..88L: Dust mass highly sensitive to assumptions
- 2016AJ....152..218I: Superantennae continuum determination ambiguity larger; HCN v2=1f detection may be contaminated by HCO+ v=0
- 2016ApJ...816L...6D: Line window missed part of the red wing
- 2016ApJ...817..168H: Source I is outside the primary beam, giving ~50% flux uncertainty; limited resolution
- 2016ApJ...819...82S: Gas masses exclude the factor ~2 uncertainty of the luminosity ratio and alpha_CO
- 2016ApJ...819...82S: N2 metallicities may be overestimated by 0.1-0.2 dex
- 2016ApJ...820...19T: Resolution does not allow detailed analysis of ring structures.
- 2016ApJ...820..118Z: Extinction correction of Pa-alpha uncertain; radio image of limited quality
- 2016ApJ...820L..39N: Higher-resolution data would be needed to confirm absence of substructure; dynamical mass is a lower limit
- 2016ApJ...822L..10I: Only one pointing; star-forming ring at 10-15 arcsec not adequately probed
- 2016ApJ...822L..10I: Dense mass has large potential uncertainty
- 2016ApJ...823...68S: Missing short spacings; fluxes are lower limits; outflow mass highly uncertain
- 2016ApJ...823...91S: Midplane snowline result is model dependent.
- 2016ApJ...823...91S: Ring not seen in 6-5 data, possibly due to sensitivity.
- 2016ApJ...823L..18H: Thermal vs non-thermal desorption contributions not constrained; narrow optically thick dust rings need higher resolution
- 2016ApJ...824...88O: Residual rms has no statistical meaning; mass strongly degenerate with inclination
- 2016ApJ...824...88O: Resolution insufficient to distinguish accretion shock from protostellar heating
- 2016ApJ...825...44I: Rotational transitions within v=0 and v2=1 not treated; same-region assumption is simplistic
- 2016ApJ...827...34O: Gas mass from a single mid-J CO line is highly uncertain; low-J CO needed
- 2016ApJ...827...81I: Small, inhomogeneous samples; tentative results; fixed eta and uncertainties not fully included
- 2016ApJ...827...81I: Most CNDs unresolved so Sigma_dense not measured
- 2016ApJ...828...46A: Gas masses depend inversely on assumed [CO]/[H2] and isotopologue ratios; CO depletion would raise gas masses
- 2016ApJ...829....6W: CO mass assumes optically thin LTE and could be larger by a factor of a few or more
- 2016ApJ...829....6W: Debris mass depends strongly on assumed size distribution, density, albedo
- 2016ApJ...829L..11P: Modest S/N and substantial ALMA-HST astrometric uncertainty
- 2016ApJ...829L..11P: Small sample
- 2016ApJ...830L..37I: COM distribution is not resolved; acetone detection tentative; angular resolution insufficient to see distribution trends
- 2016ApJ...831..161K: Missing short spacings could underestimate CO flux; data could not be combined with single-dish.
- 2016ApJ...831..161K: Cannot separate direct radial impact from shear-driven shocks.
- 2016ApJ...832..142Z: Outflow, bar and spiral arms degenerate; resolution of 2–3" limits comparison and detail
- 2016ApJ...832..142Z: Far W cloud needs higher resolution or more CO transitions to confirm
- 2016ApJ...832..204Y: Enhancement is lower at radii smaller than the beam, and depends on accurate Vk
- 2016ApJ...833L...6C: Large structures (>~12") undersampled in Band 7; could matter for dust
- 2016ApJ...833L...6C: Dust mass may be underestimated since warm dust dominates SED peak; LMC X_CO may overestimate gas
- 2016MNRAS.458L..29C: Dust mass relies on ISM grain size distribution assumption that may not hold for large-grain-dominated disc; detailed modelling deferred
- 2016MNRAS.458L..29C: Red-shifted CO side affected by cloud filtering
- 2016MNRAS.460..627K: Missing flux from lack of short spacings; masses are lower limits; age is an extreme lower limit
- 2016MNRAS.460..673N: Lack of large-distance coverage prevents associating red-shifted arcs into spirals
- 2016MNRAS.461..385B: Not a single best-fit model; outer disc emission over-predicted; SED modelling degenerate
- 2016MNRAS.462L.101A: Inclinations reflect bulk geometry; uncertainties exclude systematics; small sample
- 2016MNRAS.463..252B: Herschel photometry may include extended emission biasing SFR high; mid-IR Spitzer central pixels may be saturated
- 2016NatAs...1E...3P: Beam size precludes accurate modelling of velocity shear
- 2016PASJ...68..103F: Beam does not resolve the cloud; higher resolution and sensitivity needed
- 2017A&A...597A..32V: Limited resolution cannot distinguish gap from ring
- 2017A&A...599A..63S: Spherical symmetry ignores east-west asymmetry from binary companion
- 2017A&A...601A..49B: Only five clean lines, so detection tentative
- 2017A&A...601A..49B: Models overproduce NH2CHO and CH3CONH2 by more than an order of magnitude
- 2017A&A...601L...3P: CH2NH blending likely negligible; dust values may be higher in compact region
- 2017A&A...602A..11P: Galaxy unresolved; outflows could be missed; needs higher resolution
- 2017A&A...602A..59C: Low number statistics; no model fits so stellar masses unconstrained
- 2017A&A...603A..10B: Mass estimates are lower limits due to optical depth and >99% flux filtered out
- 2017A&A...603A..10B: Central mass cannot be determined from pv diagrams
- 2017A&A...604A...2S: Resolution too poor to separate the two nuclei
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Inner 50 AU cannot be modeled due to low resolution and dust optical depth
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Matched-filter fluxes are only lower limits
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Parameterized models include no chemistry; formation route cannot be distinguished
- 2017A&A...606A.125S: N2D+ is weak, on edge of atmospheric feature, continuum subtraction less accurate
- 2017A&A...606A.125S: Isothermal vertical temperature assumption and no vertical abundance distribution
- 2017A&A...607A..55V: Dust temperature is likely overestimated so dust mass is a lower limit
- 2017A&A...608A..22A: Decorrelation implies Tb may be higher; short observation limits sensitivity

