## Paper excerpts (40 of 413, chosen for detail and spread over fields/years)

### 2017A&A...606A.125S: DCO<SUP>+</SUP>, DCN, and N<SUB>2</SUB>D<SUP>+</SUP> reveal three different deuteration regimes in the disk around the Herbig Ae star HD 163296 (2017; protoplanetary_disks, astrochemistry; observational_alma_primary)
- question: Constrain the radial extent of DCO+, DCN and N2D+ in the HD 163296 disk and spatially characterize the high and low temperature deuteration pathways
- step 1: Keplerian-masked integrated intensity maps
  - method: Mask pixels in each channel whose projected Keplerian velocity matches the channel Doppler shift, convolved with beam, then integrate [Appendix Keplerian Masking: "we first calculate the projected radial velocity on each pixel using a stellar mass value of 2.3 M$_\odot$"]
  - software: CASA
  - parameter: stellar mass 2.3 Msun [Appendix Keplerian Masking: "using a stellar mass value of 2.3 M$_\odot$ (cite: vandenAncker1997)"]
  - validation: S/N gain of ~2 compared to Yen2016 stacking factor ~4 [Appendix Keplerian Masking: "In contrast our method achieves an increase in S/N of a factor of $\sim$ 2"]
- step 5: Fit parametric abundance ring models
  - method: Compute emission profile from column density and Tex via Remijan equation, make 2D image, convolve with beam, minimise chi2 against integrated intensity maps [4.6 Best-fit parameters: "We minimize ${ \chi^2=(F_{\rm obs}(x,y)-F_{\rm model}(x,y))^2/\sigma(x,y)^2}$ values"]
  - parameter: DCO+: 7 parameters (Rin, R1, R2, three abundances); DCN, N2D+: Rin, Rout, X [4.4 abundance models: "Our model uses a set of seven parameters describing three regions"]
  - assumption: vertically averaged abundances, no vertical distribution [4.6 Best-fit parameters: "We do not consider a vertical distribution of the DCO$^+$ and DCN molecules."]
  - fitting: chi2 minimum of the explored parameter space; formal errors at 90% confidence [Table 3: "The formal errors are calculated at 90% confidence levels."]
  - validation: Compared different DCO+ ring/gap configurations; degeneracy acknowledged [4.6 Best-fit parameters: "In the case of DCO$^+$ the location of the different radial zones are degenerate."]
- result: DCO+ integrated intensity = 1270.45 ± 5.8 mJy km/s [Table 1 (lines): "| DCO$^+$ J=3–2 | 216.112 | 1270.45$\pm$ 5.8 |"]
- result: DCN integrated intensity = 104.4 ± 5.6 mJy km/s [Table 1 (lines): "| DCN J=3–2 | 217.238 | 104.4$\pm$ 5.6 |"]
- result: N2D+ integrated intensity = 61.6 ± 7.5 mJy km/s [Table 1 (lines): "| N$_2$D$^+$ J= 3–2 | 231.321 | 61.6$\pm$ 7.5 |"]
- result: DCO+ ring radii Rin, R1, R2, Rout = 50, 118, 245, 316 ± +5/-3, +4/-5, +3/-13, +3/-10 AU [4.6 Best-fit parameters: "$R_{\rm in}$=50$^{+5}_{-3}$ AU, $R_1$=118$^{+4}_{-5}$ AU , $R_2$=245$^{+3}_{-13}$ AU and $R_{\rm out}$=316$^{+3}_{-10}$ AU"]
- result: DCN ring Rin, Rout = 51, 201 ± +/-6, +15/-24 AU [Table 3: "| $R_{\rm in}$ | 51$^{+6}_{-6}$ AU | 139$^{+5}_{-4}$ AU | 50$^{+5}_{-3}$ AU |"]
- result: N2D+ ring Rin, Rout = 139, 287 ± +5/-4, +15/-21 AU [Table 3: "| $R_{\rm out}$ | 201$^{+15}_{-24}$ AU | 287$^{+15}_{-21}$ AU | 316$^{+3}_{-10}$ AU |"]
- result: DCN abundance Xhigh = 7.5e-13 ± +/-0.9e-13 relative to H2 [4.6 Best-fit parameters: "constant abundance $X_{\rm high}$=7.5$^{+0.9}_{-0.9}\times$10$^{-13}$"]
- limitation (authors): N2D+ is weak, on edge of atmospheric feature, continuum subtraction less accurate [2 Observations: "The N$_2$D$^+$ ($J$=3–2) emission is sitting on the edge of a strong atmospheric feature at high $T_{\rm sys}$."]
- limitation (authors): Isothermal vertical temperature assumption and no vertical abundance distribution [4.4 Line excitation: "A drawback of this approach is that assuming an isothermal vertical structure of the temperature profile might not properly describe the vertical region over which the molecules extend."]
- not stated (card): CASA version; tclean/CLEAN parameters: cell size, image size, threshold, masks, channel width of cubes; Line-free channels for DCO+ and DCN continuum subtraction; Exact self-calibration solution intervals; Stellar parameters/ RADMC inputs (only referenced to Mathews2013); Fitting algorithm and parameter grid for chi2 minimisation; Inclination and position angle used for Keplerian mask and annuli

### 2019PASJ...71...85M: Complex distribution and velocity field of molecular gas in NGC 1316 as revealed by the Morita Array of ALMA (2019; nearby_galaxies, agn_and_quasars; observational_alma_primary)
- question: What are the distribution, total mass and velocity field of molecular gas in the cD/radio galaxy NGC 1316, what is its origin (inflow or outflow), and how does it interact with the nuclear jet?
- step 2: Detect CO emission and make moment maps
  - method: SoFiA source finding with noise normalisation, smoothing kernels, 4 sigma threshold, friends-of-friends merging, reliability cuts; moment 1/2 blanked below 0.9 Jy/beam km/s [2.3 Moment maps: CO emission search wit…: "build a detection mask which includes voxels outside the 4 $\sigma$ range in at least one of the convolved cubes"]
  - software: SoFiA
  - parameter: merging radius 2 pixels, 3 channels; min size 3 pixels/channels; integrated S/N>3; dilation 2 pixels, 1 channel [2.3 Moment maps: CO emission search wit…: "remove from the detection mask all objects with an integrated S/N below 3;"]
- step 3: Derive total molecular gas mass
  - method: Sum moment-0 flux in a box, convert Jy/beam to K via Rayleigh-Jeans, apply X_CO and helium factor 1.36; error from noise map [3.1 Total molecular gas mass: "The error for the molecular mass is calculated with a noise map as $\sigma_{rms} \sqrt{npts} ({\rm pixel\ scale})^2$"]
  - parameter: Box 120"x160", 114.497-114.73 GHz (1406.8-2013.55 km/s) [3.1 Total molecular gas mass: "enclosed with a box centered on (R.A., Dec.)$_{\rm ICRS}=(03^{h}22^{m}41^{s}.448, -37^{\circ}12'16''.2)$ with a width of 120 arcsec and a height of 160 arcsec"]
  - assumption: Milky-Way X_CO = 2.0e20 cm^-2 (K km/s)^-1; distance 20.8 Mpc [3.1 Total molecular gas mass: "standard CO-to-H$_2$ conversion factor of the Milky-Way of $X_{\rm CO}=2.0\times 10^{20}$ cm$^{-2}$ (K km s$^{-1}$)$^{-1}$"]
  - validation: Compared with previous single-dish masses [3.1 Total molecular gas mass: "The obtained molecular gas mass is comparable to the previous single-dish observations"]
- step 4: Characterise velocity field with PV cuts and compare with Keck ionized gas
  - method: Moment-1/2 maps and position-velocity cuts of CO; Keck/LRIS long-slit spectra PV maps compared at same PA [3.3.1 CO velocity field: "In Figure [5](#fig:pv_maps), the position-velocity (PV) maps are presented."]
  - parameter: LRIS slit PA 158.56 deg, 1.0" slit, velocity accuracy ~100 km/s [2.4 Keck/LRIS observations and data red…: "The slit is set to cross the galaxy center with P.A. of 158.56 deg."]
- result: Total molecular gas mass (Galactic X_CO) = 5.62e8 ± 0.53e8 Msun [3.1 Total molecular gas mass: "The total molecular gas mass is estimated to be $(5.62 \pm 0.53)\times 10^8$ M$_\odot$"]
- result: Central CO peak intensity = 26.8 mK at ~1720 km/s (4.2 sigma) ± not stated mK [3.2 Spatial distribution: "a weak and narrow CO emission is detected with a peak intensity of $26.8$ mK at $\sim 1720$ km s$^{-1}$"]
- result: Velocity difference NW Shell-SE Blob = ~400 ± not stated km/s [3.3.1 CO velocity field: "The velocity difference between the NW Shell and the SE Blob ($\sim 400$ km s$^{-1}$"]
- result: Molecular gas velocity dispersion = 20-50 ± not stated km/s [3.3.1 CO velocity field: "The velocity dispersion of the molecular gas is roughly in the range of $20-50$ km s$^{-1}$ at kpc-resolution."]
- limitation (authors): Keck velocity accuracy only ~100 km/s; IFU data needed [2.4 Keck/LRIS observations and data red…: "Uncertainty in absolute wavelength calibration of the data is $\lesssim2$ Å, roughly corresponding to an absolute value of velocities of $\sim100$ km s$^{-1}$."]
- limitation (authors): Line-of-sight ordering and jet inclination hard to determine [4.1 Relative line-of-sight location of …: "it is difficult to estimate it with our current data set."]
- not stated (card): Spatial cell size and image size of the cube; Which channels were used for the final 9.9 km/s binning and the TP feathering scaling factor; Line-free channels and continuum subtraction method; Dust-mass and HI inputs and the exact GDR calculation; Keck/LRIS PV extraction details and reduction software

### 2018ApJ...869...59W: Physical and Chemical Conditions of the Protostellar Envelope and the Protoplanetary Disk in HL Tau (2018; star_formation, protoplanetary_disks, astrochemistry; multi_facility_alma_minor)
- question: What are the physical and chemical conditions (gas motions, gas and dust masses, gas-to-dust ratio, CO depletion) of the protostellar envelope and the protoplanetary disk in HL Tau?
- step 4: Fit geometrically thin Keplerian disk to HCO+ channel maps
  - method: Minimum chi2 fit of Keplerian model to high-velocity HCO+ channel maps with free Mstar, PA, inclination [4.1.2 Keplerian Disk Modeling: "we performed minimum $\chi^2$ fitting of the geometrically-thin Keplerian disk model to the ALMA velocity channel maps of the HCO$^{+}$ (1–0) line at the high-velocity of $|\Delta V| > 3$ km s$^{-1}$"]
  - parameter: Fit velocity ranges V_LSR = 2.5-4.0 and 10.0-11.5 km/s; sigma = 0.4 km/s; vsys = 7 km/s [4.1.2 Keplerian Disk Modeling: "The velocity ranges of the fitting are restricted to $V_{LSR}$ = 2.5 - 4.0 km $s^{-1}$ and 10.0 - 11.5 km s$^{-1}$"]
  - assumption: Dynamical center fixed at 2.9 mm continuum peak; moment 0 of model equal to observed [4.1.2 Keplerian Disk Modeling: "The dynamical center of the model disk is fixed to be the peak position of the 2.9 mm continuum emission, and $v_{\rm sys}$ is set to be 7 km s$^{-1}$."]
  - fitting: chi2 minimization over Mstar, theta, i [4.1.2 Keplerian Disk Modeling: "The fitting parameters are thus $M_{\star}$, $\theta$, and $i$"]
