  - assumption: Ring emission axisymmetric; PA fixed to 62 deg (SAO 206462) and 16 deg (SR 21) [Analysis: "In our modeling the ring emission is assumed to be axisymmetric."]
  - fitting: Affine-invariant MCMC (emcee), minimizing chi^2 [Analysis: "The best-fit model was found by minimizing the $\chi^2$ statistic using the latest implementation of the affine-invariant MCMC *emcee* software"]
  - validation: Compared reduced chi^2 and residual maps of ring vs ring+vortex [Analysis: "The addition of a vortex prescription in the fitting improves the resulting residual map and $\chi^2$ of the fit"]
- result: Asymmetry contrast SAO 206462 = 1.5 ± 0.02 dimensionless [Observational Results: "$1.5\pm0.02$ in SAO 206462 and $1.9\pm0.01$ in SR 21"]
- result: Asymmetry contrast SR 21 = 1.9 ± 0.01 dimensionless [Observational Results: "$1.5\pm0.02$ in SAO 206462 and $1.9\pm0.01$ in SR 21"]
- result: Reduced chi^2 ring vs ring+vortex, SAO 206462 = 1.18 vs 1.05 ± not stated dimensionless [Table 2: "$\chi^2_{red}=1.18$ | $\chi^2_{red}=1.05$"]
- result: Reduced chi^2 ring vs ring+vortex, SR 21 = 1.39 vs 1.06 ± not stated dimensionless [Table 2: "$\chi^2_{red}=1.39$ | $\chi^2_{red}=1.06$"]
- result: Vortex fraction of total flux = 15% (SAO 206462), 28% (SR 21) ± not stated percent [Discussion: "The vortex encompasses 15% of the total flux density for SAO 206462 and 28% for SR 21."]
- result: Vortex aspect ratio SAO 206462 / SR 21 = 7.1 / 2.8 ± not stated dimensionless [Discussion: "$\sigma_{\phi,V}/\sigma_{r,V}=7.1$ for SAO 206462 and $\sigma_{\phi,V}/\sigma_{r,V}=2.8$ for SR 21"]
- result: Ring radius (ring+vortex) = 65.3 AU (SAO 206462), 35.0 AU (SR 21) ± 0.1 AU AU [Table 2: "$65.3\pm0.1$"]
- limitation (authors): Emission may be partly optically thick so asymmetries may not trace mass; masses are lower limits. [Discussion: "These are lower limits on the vortex mass, given the uncertainty in optical depth at this wavelength."]
- not stated (card): CASA version; Self-calibration solution intervals and reference antenna; Cell size, image size, deconvolver and masking; MCMC walkers, steps, burn-in, priors and parameter bounds; Flux calibrator model for Titan and flux uncertainty; How the moment maps were made (channel range, clip); Continuum channel selection / line-free channels

